WEBVTT

00:13:57.781 --> 00:14:03.698
there was a piece
in the Manchester Guardian about it,

00:14:03.722 --> 00:14:05.587
two whole pages.

00:14:06.349 --> 00:14:09.569
And they quoted a villager

00:14:09.593 --> 00:14:12.680
who said, "This walk connects
us to the world."

00:14:12.704 --> 00:14:15.521
He said, "It was like a light
that went on in our lives --

00:14:15.545 --> 00:14:16.976
it brought us hope."

00:14:17.436 --> 00:14:19.518
And so that's what it's about.

00:14:19.542 --> 00:14:21.348
But it's not just about psychology;

00:14:21.372 --> 00:14:22.848
it's about economics.

00:14:22.872 --> 00:14:25.976
Because as people walk, they spend money.

00:14:26.000 --> 00:14:28.976
And this woman right here, Um Ahmad,

00:14:29.000 --> 00:14:32.150
is a woman who lives on the path
in Northern Jordan.